<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 30px; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 32px; padding-bottom: 20px; width: 100%;"> <p style="margin: 0px; text-align: center;">4 strategies to boost</p> <p style="margin: 0px; text-align: center;">higher education affordability</p> </td> 
</tr> 
<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" class="aligned-bullets" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 16px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 24px; padding-bottom: 40px; width: 100%;"> <p style="margin: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px;">Affordability is a hot topic in the world of Higher Education as many experts debate on whether or not a college education is beneficial in today’s society. Despite news of declining enrollment rates, <strong>83% of people between the ages of 12-26 surveyed by Gallup think that college education is important</strong>. With a strong desire to pursue education, institutions need better strategies to help make this possible.</span></p> <p style="margin: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px;"><br />In our new playbook, we highlight strategic advice and case studies from industry experts to help you move the needle on affordability.</span></p> </td> 
